# Generated by `npm install --package-lock-only` against the pinned upstream
# commit; see the refresh recipe in Containerfile. Never hand-edited, so it is
# marked generated and collapsed by default in forge review UIs.
#
# Deliberately NOT `-diff`. THREAT_MODEL.md leans on this file as the control
# that a rebuild resolves the same bytes, and the only automated staleness check
# compares version strings — which proves the lockfile CLAIMS a release, not
# that its resolved graph came from one. `-diff` would render a regeneration as
# "Binary files ... differ", hiding exactly the thing a reviewer needs to see in
# a ref bump: which of the resolved packages or integrity hashes moved.
container/context-mode-package-lock.json linguist-generated=true
